# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
# Intentfile (A2ML Canonical) — north-star contractile for progblocks
# Author: Jonathan D.A. Jewell (hyperpolymath)
#
# Semantics: North-star contractile. Declares BOTH concrete committed
#            next-actions AND horizon aspirations the project wishes to
#            become.
#              intents — "we WILL do this; track progress"
#              wishes  — "we WISH this were true; revisit later"
#            Non-gating — this is a report, not a gate. See
#            contractiles/must/Mustfile.a2ml for hard gates.

@abstract:
North-star contractile for progblocks, a dependency-free web component for
rich code blocks in technical documentation. Currently pre-alpha: the
component now registers reliably (a prior fatal import bug is fixed and
guarded — see contractiles/bust/Bustfile.a2ml), but several
README-advertised features do not exist yet.
@end

## Purpose

Ship a small, honestly-documented, dependency-free web component that can be
dropped into any documentation site or wiki, matching what FACTS.md
verifies rather than what README.md aspires to.

## Anti-Purpose

This repository is NOT:
- A syntax highlighter
- A static site generator
- A Markdown parser
- A full A2ML implementation — the parser is a stub
- A vehicle for claiming a feature before the code implements it

## If In Doubt

If you are unsure whether a change is in scope, ask. Sensitive areas:
- The innerHTML / XSS surface (see contractiles/trust/Trustfile.a2ml)
- Licence, GOVERNANCE.md
- .machine_readable/descriptiles/CLADE.a2ml (repo identity)
- progblocks-launcher.sh (generated — never hand-edit)

## Committed Next-Actions

### fatal-import-fixed
- description: The validateK9 named-import mismatch is fixed (customElements.define runs) and a registration test guards against it recurring
- run: "! grep -q 'import { validateK9 }' src/prog-block.js"
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: tests/registration.test.js (asserts customElements.get('prog-block') is defined), plus this probe
- status: achieved

### just-test-can-fail
- description: Justfile's test recipe reports failure honestly; the `|| echo "No tests configured yet"` fallback that swallowed it has been removed
- run: "! grep -q 'No tests configured yet' Justfile"
- severity: critical
- enforced-by: this probe, plus visual confirmation that `Justfile`'s `test:` recipe is a bare `node --test`
- status: achieved

### package-json-present
- description: A real package.json (ESM, dev dependencies, lockfile) exists so npm ci has something to install
- run: test -f package.json
- severity: warning
- enforced-by: this probe
- status: achieved

## Wishes

### Near Horizon

#### xss-remediation
- description: Escape or otherwise neutralise the unescaped-innerHTML injection surface before this component is used on any real documentation site
- horizon: near
- status: declared

#### focus-preserving-render
- description: Stop rewriting the whole shadow root on every keystroke so variable inputs are actually typeable
- horizon: near
- status: declared

### Mid Horizon

#### real-a2ml-parser
- description: Replace the placeholder tree-sitter-a2ml.wasm and commented-out parse path with a real, working A2ML parser so variable substitution is backed by an actual grammar instead of a bare regex
- horizon: mid
- status: declared

#### working-preview-toggle
- description: Build the code/preview view toggle README.md already advertises but src/prog-block.js does not implement
- horizon: mid
- status: declared

### Far Horizon

#### templating-wizards
- description: Storage-backed templating wizards — currently no storage, no forms, and no wizard code exists anywhere in the tree
- horizon: far
- status: declared

#### live-linter
- description: Wire view-manager.js's real (currently unused) WebSocket/linter code into the rendered linter panel, replacing the hardcoded '<i>Linter ready</i>' string
- horizon: far
- status: declared
